### Run a command when a timer finishes

One of Peaclock's more useful features is `timer-exec`. For example, its sample configurations use a notification command:

Bash

```
timer-exec 'notify-send -a peaclock "timer complete"'
```

This allows a countdown to trigger a shell command when it completes. What happens depends on the command you configure and the programs available on your system. The example uses `notify-send`, commonly associated with Linux desktop notifications; it is not a universal macOS notification command.

You can also clear the configured action by setting its value to an empty string.

