## 10. What else does Peaclock provide?

Beyond the main modes and commands, these are the other documented capabilities.

Responsive terminal layout

Automatically adapts to terminal dimensions, or uses a chosen aspect ratio to prevent the clock from looking stretched.

Locale-aware date and time

Configurable locale, timezone and date-format string.

Runtime customization

Change the mode, view, dimensions, colors, display options and timer settings while the application is running.

Persistent command history

Save past commands, navigate matching history entries and use fuzzy searching.

Timer completion actions

Execute a configured shell command when a countdown finishes.

Portable, text-based configuration

Store settings in a file, maintain reusable presets and export the current configuration using `mkconfig`.

The original project documents support for Linux, BSD and macOS. It uses terminal control sequences for cursor movement, styling and screen clearing, so the exact rendering can vary with terminal compatibility.

